member.summary:
Ability activation payload. Gameplay owns the shape and its serialization;
the engine only moves the argument vector, so no gameplay type reaches the
public Ability API. No reflection: each payload writes and reads itself.

Explicit six-state transitions. Instant effects fold same tick.
Edges are evaluated by NativeCore lumio-hfsm via ;
this type does not walk a C# switch.

Effect parameter payload. Gameplay owns the shape and its fields;
the engine only passes the parameters to the effect implementation and extracts
the magnitude and fx_key for settlement and client RPC notification.

Explicit eight-state transitions. Instant abilities fold same tick.
Edges are evaluated by NativeCore lumio-hfsm via ;
this type does not walk a C# switch.
